# Milestone: v0.10.12-cat-e-activation
# Covers: cross-spec chain: cond watcher fires -> body emits event -> event
#         subscriber fires; at(x > threshold) body emits e!, at(e?) logs.
#         Tests that a rising-edge cond watcher can trigger event dispatch
#         as a downstream effect (spec cross-spec §2.2).
# matrix-row: reactive-at-cond
#
# Activation history: Cat. E re-audit D2 ratified at v0.10.12.  The original
# 'blocked: chain does not propagate' label was unsubstantiated by C-level
# evidence (c_event_emit_async is non-allocating + body-strand-safe + unit-
# tested via test_event_emit_async.c).  Activated empirically via Realm.x = v
# capture (the v0.10.10 W3 pattern).
#
# Install order: threshold starts at 0 (cond false at install); at(threshold>3)
# does not fire immediately.  Trigger sets Realm.threshold = 10 via a nested
# call which provides the safepoint urbi_vm_watcher_eval_dirty needs.  The at-cond
# body runs e! which enqueues the at(e?) subscriber body; that body runs and
# sets Realm.log = "event" before Realm.log is read.

var Realm.log = ""
[00000000] ""

var threshold = 0
[00000001] 0

var e = Event.new()
[00000002] <event>

at (e?) Realm.log = "event"
[00000003] nil

at (threshold > 3) e!
[00000004] nil

var trigger = function() { Realm.threshold = 10 }; trigger()
[00000005] 10

Realm.log
[00000006] "event"
